WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.110
- [Instructor] Let's say
that we want to figure out

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:07.110
what is seven and 11/12
minus one and 6/12.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.363
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.750
All right now let's work on this together.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.350
So there's a couple of ways
that you could approach this.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:23.350
You can view this as the same
thing as seven plus 11/12

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:29.480
and then minus one and you
might be tempted to say minus

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.900
one and then plus 6/12 but
remember you're subtracting

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.630
not just the one you're
subtracting one and you're

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:39.520
subtracting 6/12 so minus one minus 6/12.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.240
Now why is that useful to
think about it that way?

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.490
Well now you can think about
the whole numbers so you can

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:50.490
say this is going to be
seven minus one plus 11/12,

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:55.790
plus 11/12 minus 6/12, minus 6/12.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:01.160
And so seven minus one is six,
so it's going to be six plus

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:04.090
now if I have 11 of
something in this case 12ths

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.770
and I'm subtracting six of
them away six of the 12ths,

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:10.620
I'm gonna be left with five of
those somethings, five 12ths.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:14.450
So it's going to be six plus
5/12 which is the same thing

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:18.540
as six and 5/12.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.400
Now as you get more used
to this you could do some

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.130
of this maybe even in your
head, you could say hey look,

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:27.130
look at the whole number
parts, seven minus one is going

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:32.470
to give me six and then
if I say 11/12 minus 6/12

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:36.240
is going to give me 5/12 so
that takes up a little bit

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.190
less space.

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:39.385
Another way that you might
see this approached is you can

00:01:39.385 --> 00:01:44.385
rewrite this as seven and 11/12
minus, minus one and 6/12.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:55.080
Let me do the 6/12 in that
blue color that I'm using

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:59.500
for the fraction parts,
6/12 and then I would first

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:03.162
focus on the fractional parts
and I'd say 11/12 minus 6/12

00:02:03.162 --> 00:02:08.162
is 5/12 and seven minus one
is six and I got six and 5/12.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.830
So many different ways to
approach the same thing

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:15.350
and at the end of the day
they really are the same

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:17.563
underlying idea.

